      {
        "review_id": 148066851,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r148066851-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Interesting but very dirty",
        "text": "The temple is something you should see on a visit, as it is the holiest place in Hinduism, but be prepared for filth. The grounds are littered with trash, burning waste, and burning bodies. \n\nYou can witness cremations happening right in front of you on wooden pyres. Out of respect, we took very few photos and only when we knew it was ok. The families of the deceased light the fires and in most cases their relative has died only hours before. \n\nWe hired one of the numerous guides to tell us about the temple and I would actually advise it. They do know a lot and its fun to talk to them. But negotiate a price before. A reasonable price is around ten dollars US, paid at the end. If your guide goes above and beyond, feel free to give a small tip as extra. Our guide was great, but if you don't like any that approach you, just waive them off until you find someone you like.\n\nThere is a lot of history here and its worth a look.",
        "review_tip": null,
