        "title": "Most sacred temple",
        "text": "Shri Pashupatinath temple is one of the most sacred of the hindu temples, is the Lord Shiva temple. \n\nIt is said that this is over 2000 years old and is very unique due to its architecture and also the story of its existance.\n\nOnly hindu religion people are allowed to enter the temple. The priests of the temple have always been from India for generations, and it continues.\n\nMonday is the sacred day of Lord Shiva, and therefore many devotees from Nepal and abroad visit the temple.\n\nCarrying mobile phones, camera and any article made from leather is strictly prohibited. There are lockers provided free of cost, to safely store your belongings.\n\nThere is one main temple, surrounded by several smaller temples in the main premises. A huge 'nandi' bull is seen facing lord shiva.\n\nThe main Shiv lingam has four faces of Lord Shiva in four directions. \n\n",
